   INTRODUCTION
   ============================================================================

   QFront is a FidoNet front-end mailer and mail processor for PCBoard
   15.3 and 15.4 bulletin board systems. It answers the phone, determines
   whether the caller is a FidoNet mailer or a human, and acts accordingly:

     - FidoNet mailer: runs a FidoNet session (EMSI or YooHoo handshake,
       Zmodem file transfer), exchanges mail packets and files, hangs up.

     - Human caller: exits with errorlevel 1 so BOARD.BAT can load
       PCBoard to handle the caller. The modem connection stays up.

     - FAX call: exits with errorlevel 5 so BOARD.BAT can route to FAX
       software.

   Between calls, QFront scans the BSO (Binkley Style Outbound) directory
   for pending outbound mail and dials the destination nodes.

   This is a clean-room implementation. No code from the original QFront
   v1.20a by Rob Kittredge / RoCo Software was used. All protocol support
   was written from the public FidoNet Technical Standards (FTS) documents.

   QFront v1.0.0 compiles under OpenWatcom 2.0 (DOS4G) and GCC (Linux).


   DIFFERENCES FROM THE ORIGINAL QFRONT
   ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

   The original QFront v1.20a was written for Wildcat! BBS. This version
   is written for PCBoard. Key differences:

     - PCBoard integration via BOARD.BAT errorlevels (not Wildcat! hooks)
     - Text config file (qfront.cfg) instead of binary QFCONFIG.DAT
     - Nodelist compiled to .NDX binary index (same as original)
     - Uses binkd as external mailer for BinkP/IP sessions
     - Built-in EMSI, YooHoo, Zmodem, Xmodem for modem sessions
     - Runs on DOS (via DOS4G extender) and Linux
     - GPLv3 licensed — source code included


                                QFront v1.0.0
                                   Page 2

   WHAT'S INCLUDED — PROGRAMS
   ============================================================================

   The QFront package contains five programs:

   QFRONT.EXE    The main mailer. Sits on the COM port waiting for calls,
                 handles FidoNet sessions, polls outbound nodes, and exits
                 with errorlevels for BOARD.BAT. This is the program that
                 runs in your BBS batch file loop.

   QFCONFIG.EXE  Configuration editor. Full-screen TUI (text user interface)
                 for editing qfront.cfg. Supports all settings: addresses,
                 paths, modem strings, events, areas, nodes, routing, file
                 requests, semaphores, function keys, and more.

                 You can also edit qfront.cfg directly with a text editor.

   QSCAN.EXE     EchoMail tosser and scanner. Processes inbound .PKT files
                 into your message base (toss), and scans your message base
                 for outbound echomail to pack into .PKT files (scan).

                 Also handles Areafix robot messages (subscribe/unsubscribe
                 to echomail areas via netmail commands).

   QNLIST.EXE    Nodelist compiler. Applies nodediffs to your raw nodelist,
                 verifies CRC, and compiles to a binary .NDX index for fast
                 lookup. Also processes private nodelists and pointlists.

   QFUTIL.EXE    Utility program. Command-line tool for creating polls,
                 netmail messages, file requests, update requests, and file
                 attaches from batch files or the DOS command line.


   All five programs are DOS4G extended (32-bit protected mode) and require
   a DOS4GW-compatible extender. The DOS4GW.EXE stub is included.

   Linux binaries are also available (compiled with GCC, no extender needed).


                                QFront v1.0.0
                                   Page 3

   WHAT'S INCLUDED — DISPLAY FILES
   ============================================================================

   QFront includes several text files that are displayed to callers or
   used for status messages. Place these in your QFront directory:

   NORMAL.TXT    Displayed to callers during a normal FidoNet session.
   CRITICAL.TXT  Displayed during a critical (high-priority) session.
   FAILED.TXT    Displayed when a session fails.
   LOWBAUD.TXT   Displayed when the connect speed is below the minimum.
   EXPWARN.TXT   Displayed when the registration is about to expire.
                 (Not used in GPLv3 version — no registration required.)
   AREAFIX.TXT   Help text sent in response to Areafix %HELP command.


   WHAT'S INCLUDED — CONFIGURATION FILES
   ============================================================================

   qfront.cfg    Main configuration file. Plain text, one setting per line.
                 Edit with QFCONFIG.EXE or any text editor.

                 Lines starting with # or ; are comments.
                 Blank lines are ignored.

   QMAGIC.DAT    Magic filename aliases for file requests. Format:
                   ALIAS  /real/path/to/file
                 Example:
                   FILES  C:\PCB\GEN\DLPATH.LST
                   ABOUT  C:\PCB\GEN\ABOUT.ZIP

   QRLIMIT.DAT   File request limits. Format:
                   MaxBytesSession=10000000
                   MaxFilesSession=50
                   MinSpeed=9600
                   AllowUnlisted=0


